s name or were you aware of him  I heard his name before bye didn't know  I think he worked out one of the local  stores here so when I saw the picture of  him I know he looked kind of familiar  but know much about him what kind of  store is it the dollar store the dollar  store interesting did you all have you  gone through drills for a situation like  this yeah we were pretty prepared we  know too high like stay away from  windows and everything but we were  trying to do that but once though the  bullets went through the window and the  glass shattered we knew it was like the  real thing that this is not a drill or  anything and when people got hit they  were screaming they're in panic mode  they didn't know what to do so we try to  keep everyone quiet like fascism like as  quick as we can  we wanted everyone remain calm at the  time I didn't know that any students  were shot so and then someone told me my  classroom is sitting next to me but the  bullets were extremely loud nothing I  ever heard oh did you text your parents  from the classroom  I didn't have my phone at the time but  my parents knew so afterwards the the  SWAT came and they asked how many people  were injured or yeah if there's any  deaths or injuries so we told them and  how many students I think there was  about thirty students in our class so  then we all had a we all lined up one by  one  walked out we had to run as far as we  can and we all had to stay calm is  really hard watching everyone people  were crying there was a lot of blood  everywhere  leaving the hallway looking on the floor  seeing blood and just like kids just  such a scary thought when did your  parents find out you were okay once I  left my backpack and everything is down  class right now my car's there my keys I  just grabbed my phone and ran and my mom  called me a bunch of times I wasn't  answering so she was worried but then I  called her I was walking away and I was  with a bunch of kids so I felt like safe  and just walk as far as it can you're so  calm right now I can't imagine seeing  something like that how do you feel yeah  me before I was like shaking the entire  time I was shaking but now like I'm  still in shock right now it's just like  unbelievable to actually think this  happen here at Stoneman Douglas it's  have you ever felt threatened there  before  no never but I know that the staff  trained us is really going to training  us for like anything a tornado drill  hurricane drill yeah especially this so  I think everyone reacted good and the  teachers had the door locks so that was  good  was your teacher calm the whole time my  teacher was pretty calm yeah she was on  the phone she was like being quiet on  the phone so her being calm kept us all  calm but we're all like there for each  other we're all like cuddled up together  holding hands what a what a horrifying  horrifying experience you've lived  through Rebecca Bogart thanks a lot for  sharing that with us thank you
 

